# Workflow V2 — Cursor Handoff Rules

## V2.1 Two workflow systems

This project has transitioned from a V1 5-role pipeline to a V2
task-semantic pipeline. The V2 system uses:

- `features/<feature>/docs/dev_log.md` as the state machine
- `docs/reviews/<feature>/<YYYYMMDD>-discovery-review.md` for discovery
- Subagents: feature-plan, feature-review, feature-build, feature-verify,
  ship, bug-diagnose, bug-fix, bug-verify, feature-dev-loop, bugfix-loop

The V1 system (`handoff/` directory, analyze → implement → test →
summarize → ship) is **deprecated and removed**. Do not create `handoff/`
files or reference V1 agent names.

## V2.2 Handoff display — hard constraint

When executing any Workflow V2 subagent (either spawned or inline),
the **final response MUST be ONLY the `## Handoff` block** defined in
the subagent's template.

Cursor has no parent/child agent boundary — when you run a subagent's
instructions, you ARE the subagent. This makes it especially important
to follow the Output Contract:

- Do NOT add free-form prose, explanation, or commentary before or after
  the Handoff block
- Do NOT end with a question like "要继续吗？" or "是否启动下一步？"
- Do NOT strip the `## Handoff` heading or `### Next Step` section
- If you need to communicate extra context, put it inside the **Summary**
  field of the Handoff block

## V2.3 Context prefix (allowed)

If you have observations that don't fit in the Summary field, you may
place them **ABOVE** the Handoff block under a `## Context` heading.
The Handoff block itself must remain intact and unmodified below.

## V2.4 Relationship with V1

The V1 5-role system (analyze, implement, test, summarize, ship) has been
fully replaced. All V1 `.cursor/commands/` and `.cursor/rules/handoff.mdc`
(original version) are removed. This file is the V2 replacement.

## V2.5 Why this rule exists

Each subagent template contains an Output Contract that tells the model
"your final response must be only the Handoff block." But Cursor executes
subagents inline, so there's no system boundary to enforce this — the model
can easily slip into conversational mode after completing the structured work.

This rule file provides a second enforcement layer at the Cursor Rules level,
ensuring the Handoff block is always the final output regardless of how
the subagent was invoked.

**Cross-platform sync:** This rule corresponds to:
- `CLAUDE.md` §Workflow V2 Subagent Output Display (Claude Code)
- `AGENTS.md` §1 (Codex)

Changes here must be synced to those files.
